Source: pgsodium
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~), pgsodium-libsodium-dev (>= 1.0.22)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/michelp/pgsodium

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pgsodium
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pgsodium
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Modern cryptography for PostgreSQL using libsodium.
 pgsodium is an encryption extension for PostgreSQL using high-level
 cryptographic algorithms from a private, symbol-isolated libsodium build.
 It also provides Server Key Management and Transparent Column Encryption.
